@* A signed-in account without catalogService access.

   Deliberately not a sign-in link: the customer is already signed in, so offering to sign them in
   again is a loop, and what is missing is a permission rather than a session. Signing out is the way
   out, and it is the same address the header uses, so the two cannot drift apart. *@
<div class="container section stack-md">
    <h1 class="headline-lg">No access to the builder</h1>
    <p class="body-lg muted">
        Your account is signed in, but it does not carry catalogService access. Ask whoever administers
        accounts for this demonstration to grant it, or sign in as an account that has it.
    </p>
    <a class="button button--primary" href="@AccountController.SignOutPath" data-enhance-nav="false">Sign out</a>
</div>
